=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The Linux bridge interface `br0` on `switch0` is administratively/statically DOWN, disabling all L2 forwarding on that device.

**Mechanism:** `switch0` is a software bridge that binds two physical ports — `eth0` (uplink to `router0` via the `link_r0_sw0` segment) and `eth1` (downlink to the IT department's `lan_it` segment, shared by `it_hod`, `it_lab1`–`it_lab4`). The bridge `br0` is the forwarding entity; when it is DOWN the kernel stops processing frames across it, so no Ethernet frames can flow between the router-facing port and the IT LAN. IT hosts therefore cannot ARP for the gateway (192.168.1.1 on router0) and receive no replies; any off-subnet packet simply has no path.

**Localization:** `switch0`, interface `br0`. Both slave interfaces (`eth0` and `eth1`) are UP and operational; the problem is exclusively the bridge master being down. Zero carrier-changes and an empty dmesg confirm no flapping — the bridge is statically down.

**Root cause:** The bridge interface `br0` on `switch0` was brought down (or never successfully raised after a fault injection) after startup, severing the only L2 path between `router0` and the IT-department LAN; all other switch bridges (e.g., `switch1` for CS dept) remain unaffected.

**Fix:** On `switch0`, run `ip link set dev br0 up` to restore the bridge to operational state, which will immediately resume L2 forwarding between the router and all IT-department hosts.
=== END ===